        "answer": {
          "short": "Test; True for; Assume true for; $p$ is an integer; Prove true for; WTP; where $q$ is an integer; LHS; using assumption; is an integer; $9p+1$; an integer; where $q$ is an integer. Conclusion: true for all integers $n\\geq1$ by mathematical induction.",
          "worked": "Test $n=1$: $LHS=3^2-1=9-1=8$, so the statement is true for $n=1$.\n\nAssume true for $n=k$: $3^{2k}-1=8p$, where $p$ is an integer.\n\nProve true for $n=k+1$. WTP: $3^{2(k+1)}-1=8q$, where $q$ is an integer.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}LHS&=3^{2k+2}-1\\\\&=3^2\\times3^{2k}-1\\\\&=9\\times3^{2k}-1\\\\&=9(8p+1)-1\\quad\\text{using assumption}\\\\&=72p+9-1\\\\&=72p+8\\\\&=8(9p+1)\\\\&=8q\\end{aligned}$$\nSince $p$ is an integer, $q=9p+1$ is also an integer. The statement is true for $n=1$, and truth for $n=k$ implies truth for $n=k+1$. Therefore it is true for all integers $n\\geq1$ by mathematical induction.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
